{
  "requirement": "The SDK offers this `Sources` method and exposes the `search_structure`\ncommand through its source tools.\n\n```rust,ignore\nimpl Sources {\n    // ...\n\n    /// Search source structure.\n    pub async fn search_structure(\n        &self,\n        query: &StructuralQuery,\n    ) -> Result<StructuralMatches, SourceError>;\n\n    // ...\n}\n```",
  "determination": true,
  "rationale": "**Method signature.** `crates/trust-but-verify/src/sources.rs#impl[Sources]/fn[search_structure]` is `pub async fn search_structure(&self, query: &StructuralQuery) -> Result<StructuralMatches, SourceError>`. This matches the required signature exactly. It sits in `impl Sources`, and `Sources` is a public type re-exported from `lib.rs` along with `StructuralQuery`, `StructuralMatches` and `SourceError`.\n\n**Delegation and error type.** The method delegates to `SourceAnalysis::search_structure` (`sources.rs#impl[SourceAnalysis<P>]/fn[search_structure]`). That function calls `self.provider.search_structure(query, &self.languages)` and returns `P::Error`. `Sources` holds `analysis: SourceAnalysis<LocalSources>`. `impl SourceProvider for LocalSources` sets `type Error = SourceError`, so the delegated result type is exactly `Result<StructuralMatches, SourceError>`. The `SourceProvider` trait also provides `search_structure` with a default implementation.\n\n**Tool exposure.** `agent/sources.rs#impl[SourceSession<…>/ToolSession<D>]/fn[definitions]` declares a `search_structure` tool. It requires `language` and `rule` and optionally takes `prefix` and `limit`. In `fn[dispatch]`, the `\"search_structure\"` arm builds a `StructuralQuery` and calls `self.tools.analysis.search_structure(...)`. The tool is therefore exposed through the SDK's source tools and reaches the same operation.\n\n**Tests and acknowledgments.** Tests in `agent/tests.rs` exercise the tool through `dispatch`. They carry `{test}` references to the `search_structure` behavior and inputs requirements. This requirement is structural only, and no gaps or `{fixme}` acknowledgments apply.",
